course: dictionary
lesson: 4749
title: Hospital: a place of help and healing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hospital is a large building where sick or injured people are looked after by doctors and nurses. The words around a new word, its context, often give clues to its meaning. «A boy in Scotland ate shiny red berries from a bush in the park; he was sick and dizzy, and his mum had to rush him to hospital.» Sick, dizzy and rush tell you he needed help fast, so a hospital is where he got it.
explain: «Most people who go to hospital get better; hospitals are mainly places of help and healing.» Healing is a clue. It means getting better after being ill or hurt, so a hospital is a place where people are helped to heal.
explain: Hospitals have rules to keep everyone safe and calm. «In a hospital or doctor's waiting room you speak quietly and stay seated, because patients may be ill or worried.» A patient is a person being looked after by doctors, so speaking quietly shows you care about people who are resting or feeling poorly.
fact: A hospital is a large building where sick or injured people are looked after by doctors and nurses.
fact: In an emergency, a person can be taken to hospital by ambulance.
fact: Emergency numbers: call 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, or 111 in New Zealand.
fact: A&E (UK) or ER (US) is the part of a hospital that deals with emergencies.
fact: Babies are often born in hospitals, and hospitals have wards and operating theatres.
exercise: «The boy was sick and dizzy, so his mum had to rush him to hospital.» Where did his mum take him? | A park | A shop | *A hospital | A school
exercise: A teenager in Arizona was bitten by a rattlesnake and «spent days in hospital while doctors treated the swelling.» What did the doctors do? | *Treated the swelling | Played football with him | Sent him home at once | Went on holiday
exercise: Which part of a hospital deals with emergencies in the UK? | Library | *A&E | Canteen | Art room
test: Which number should you call for an ambulance in New Zealand? | UK | 000 | USA | *111
test: «Jake's dad goes into hospital and Jake is angry at everything.» What does this suggest about Jake? | He wants to be a doctor | He is bored and sleepy | *He is upset and worried about his dad | He is very happy about the hospital
exam: Why should you speak quietly in a hospital or doctor's waiting room? | Because hospitals are closed | Because the doctors are asleep | *Because patients may be ill or worried | Because the nurses cannot hear well
